    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0614" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p1/pg572"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 253</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.5–MAP/2–1651:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Italy
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d253-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-02-16T19:00:00-05:00">February 16,
                            1951—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3623. Tomap.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Fol is joint State–ECA msg.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>We have just recd Embdes 2263<anchor n="2" xml:id="d253-f2"/> and feel
                        certain respects which will be apparent Mission and Emb, it not entirely consistent Deptel 3553,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d253-f3"/> particularly para
                        4 and last sentence, para 2, latter. Note especially phrase “same amt or
                        more”.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Also concerned lest Itals receive impression they will receive firm
                        commitment econ aid for bal this fiscal year and next year before adequate
                        assurances and evidences have been presented on adequacy Ital program from
                        mil and production viewpoint, in accordance with criteria outlined para 5,
                            Deptel 3143.<anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d253-f4"/> Appreciate fully difficulty reaching conclusions
                        adequacy Ital mil program because of its present tentative state. Believe,
                        however, important <pb facs="0615" n="573" xml:id="pg573"/> retain US
                        freedom of action on aid until maximum possible assurances re fullest use
                        Ital econ resources and mounting maximum possible def production effort have
                        been obtained.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Note para I 2. language ur memo<anchor n="5" xml:id="d253-f5"/> appears
                        contemplate aid for imports only against mil expenditures which obviously
                        inconsistent Deptel 3143 and presumably
                        not intended.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>Re aid figures, wld appreciate ur recommendation before any final position
                        taken as requested Deptel 3150 to
                            Rome.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d253-f6"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d253-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d253-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Bell and Cleveland and cleared with Peterson; sent by
                    pouch to London for USDep, Paris, and
                    Heidelberg.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d253-f2" n="2" xml:id="d253-f2-content">
                <p>For the text of the memorandum by the ECA Mission
                    in Italy, which was sent to Washington as an enclosure to despatch 2263, see
                    Document 249.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d253-f3" n="3" xml:id="d253-f3-content">
                <p>Document 251.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d253-f4" n="4" xml:id="d253-f4-content">
                <p>Document 246.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d253-f5" n="5" xml:id="d253-f5-content">
                <p>The memorandum under reference is the enclosure to despatch 2263 cited in
                    footnote 2 above.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d253-f6" n="6" xml:id="d253-f6-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see footnote 14, Document 246.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
